  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRRS Mongolia (Scoping) 2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Due to the many occurrences of heavy rainfall in July and August of this year, the flood water levels of Tuul and Selbe rivers have reached a historic high. The city of Ulaanbaatar has faced multiple large-scale floods and water disasters in July and August.The request from the Governor and Mayor of Ulaanbaatar states: &#x2018;There is an eminent need to take urgent actions towards significantly improving the capital city&#x2019;s climate resilience through strengthening the structure and capacity to prevent and reduce future disaster risks, develop a comprehensive disaster management system, and the ability to quickly undertake response and reconstruction measures.&#x2019;The focus of a DRRS scoping intervention would focus on prevention, early warning and response.</narrative>
  </description>
